OL,3,GNEWSAStately homes warn over 'Halloween
OL,4,Aevent'
OL,5,
OL,6,FTwo stately homes have warned
OL,7,Fthrill-seekers to be vigilant after
OL,8,Fdiscovering  Halloween events were
OL,9,Fbeing advertised at their venues
OL,10,Fwithout their permission.
OL,12,FThe events at Burton Constable Hall in
OL,13,FSkirlaugh, East Yorkshire, and Temple
OL,14,FNewsam in Leeds were listed at
OL,15,Fhauntedhalloweenescape.co.uk.
OL,17,FAlasdair Hutson, chief executive of the
OL,18,FBurton Constable Foundation, said the
OL,19,Fevent had "nothing to do with us",
OL,20,Fwhile Leeds City Council said it "had
OL,21,Fnot been organised or authorised by our
OL,22,Fsite team".
OL,23,APub: 20-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,384,380,200,160,0,100
